ion, escape sets, minimise inventory."},{"hazard":"Corrosive materials","detail":"Cumene hydroperoxide, Phenol. Material selection, PPE, safety showers, bunded storage."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Cumene per t phenol","model":1.37325,"published":[1.31,1.38],"unit":"t/t phenol","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"EU BREF LVOC (JRC109279, 2017), Section 8.3.3","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/JRC109279_LVOC_Bref.pdf","note":"Cumene fed to the oxidisers net of recycle. Set by the oxidation selectivity, a typical design value.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":true},{"metric":"Cumene per lb phenol plus acetone","model":0.849188,"published":0.81,"unit":"lb/lb","error_pct":4.838036,"inside_range":null,"source":"US DOE, Energy and Environmental Profile of the US Chemical Industry (2000), Chapter 4 (cumene, phenol/acetone)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1218625","note":"DOE quotes the stoichiometric ratio; the model includes the AMS loss.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":true},{"metric":"Benzene per lb cumene","model":0.650546,"published":0.651,"unit":"lb/lb","error_pct":-0.069794,"inside_range":null,"source":"US DOE, Energy and Environmental Profile of the US Chemical Industry (2000), Chapter 4 (cumene, phenol/acetone)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1218625","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":3,"pass":true},{"metric":"Propylene per lb cumene","model":0.350807,"published":0.351,"unit":"lb/lb","error_pct":-0.054937,"inside_range":null,"source":"US DOE, Energy and Environmental Profile of the US Chemical Industry (2000), Chapter 4 (cumene, phenol/acetone)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1218625","note":"Polymer grade propylene; propane in refinery grade feed is not modelled.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":3,"pass":true},{"metric":"Acetone co-product per kg phenol","model":0.617133,"published":0.63,"unit":"kg/kg","error_pct":-2.042401,"inside_range":null,"source":"ecoinvent 3.6 'phenol production, from cumene' (RoW) via GLAD","url":"https://www.globallcadataaccess.org/phenol-production-cumene-upr-ecoinvent-36-allocation-cut-0","note":"Model is the 1 to 1 molar split from cleavage, 0.617 kg/kg.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":true},{"metric":"Steam use, phenol plant","model":2.21705,"published":[2.3,2.8],"unit":"t/t phenol","error_pct":-3.606502,"inside_range":false,"source":"EU BREF LVOC (JRC109279, 2017), Table 8.5","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/JRC109279_LVOC_Bref.pdf","note":"Model steam for the phenol section only (concentrator and the three column systems), before the credit from burning AMS. Reflux ratios are typical design values.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":25,"pass":true},{"metric":"Electricity, phenol plant","model":206.675917,"published":[190,326],"unit":"kWh/t phenol","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"EU BREF LVOC (JRC109279, 2017), Table 8.5","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/JRC109279_LVOC_Bref.pdf","note":"Model covers the whole plant including the cumene unit; the air compressor dominates.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":25,"pass":true},{"metric":"Net process energy, phenol/acetone","model":1648.89978,"published":[6020,9680],"unit":"Btu/lb phenol + acetone","error_pct":-72.609638,"inside_range":false,"source":"US DOE, Energy and Environmental Profile of the US Chemical Industry (2000), Chapter 4 (cumene, phenol/acetone)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1218625","note":"Phenol section steam at an 85% efficient boiler plus electricity at 3,412 Btu/kWh. The model reads far below the US 1997 average even though its steam sits near the EU BREF plant; the DOE figure includes fuel oil, coal and other purchased energy for older, less integrated plants. Left failing.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":25,"pass":false},{"metric":"Fixed capital, scaled from published plant","model":150113799.617437,"published":430118556.745483,"unit":"USD (2024)","error_pct":-65.099437,"inside_range":null,"source":"ChemNet News (19 Oct 2026): Haldia Petrochemicals phenol plant, 345,000 t/y phenol and 215,000 t/y acetone, Lummus technology, total investment INR 60 billion, about USD 630 million. Scaled with exponent 0.7, not escalated (CEPCI table ends at 2024)","url":"https://news.chemnet.com/news-10860.html","note":"The published figure is a total investment in India, including offsites, a cumene unit and owner's costs; the model is a US grassroots Turton estimate.","kind":"capex","tolerance_pct":50,"pass":false}],"assumptions":["Oxidation selectivity 93% to cumene hydroperoxide; the rest is lumped as dimethylbenzyl alcohol, which dehydrates to AMS and water in the cleavage. Acetophenone and other minor by-products are not modelled.","Cleavage is taken as complete and fully selective to phenol and acetone.","Alkylator makes 90% cumene and the rest DIPB on propylene; 98% of the DIPB is transalkylated back to cumene and the rest leaves as heavies.","Propylene is polymer grade; benzene is pure.","Sulphuric acid catalyst (tens of ppm) and the caustic used to neutralise it are too small to show as streams.","Cumene carried by the oxidiser off gas is recovered by chilling and carbon adsorption and not counted as a loss.","AMS and heavies are burnt in the site boiler for steam; many plants hydrogenate AMS back to cumene or sell it.","Column duties from reflux ratio times latent heat; reflux ratios are typical design values, not one plant's."],"notes":[]}